sn35.154:1.3 | S: How is someone accomplished in the faculties defined?” | T: In what way, venerable sir, is one equipped with faculties?”
sn35.154:2.1 | S: “Mendicant, if someone meditates observing rise and fall in the eye faculty, they grow disillusioned with the eye faculty. | T: “If, bhikkhu, while one dwells contemplating rise and fall in the eye faculty, one experiences revulsion towards the eye faculty;
sn35.154:2.2 | S: If they meditate observing rise and fall in the ear faculty … nose faculty … tongue faculty … body faculty … | T: if, while one dwells contemplating rise and fall in the ear faculty, one experiences revulsion towards the ear faculty; …
sn35.154:2.3 | S: mind faculty, they grow disillusioned with the mind faculty. | T: if, while one dwells contemplating rise and fall in the mind faculty, one experiences revulsion towards the mind faculty,
sn35.154:2.4 | S: Being disillusioned, desire fades away. … When they’re freed, they know they’re freed. | T: then, experiencing revulsion, one becomes dispassionate…. When the mind is liberated, there comes the knowledge: ‘It’s liberated.’
sn35.154:2.5 | S: They understand: ‘Rebirth is ended, the spiritual journey has been completed, what had to be done has been done, there is nothing further for this place.’ | T: One understands: ‘Destroyed is birth, the holy life has been lived, what had to be done has been done, there is no more for this state of being.’
sn35.154:2.6 | S: This is how someone who is accomplished in the faculties is defined.” | T: It is in this way, bhikkhu, that one is equipped with faculties.”
sn35.154:2.7 | P: Navamaṁ. | T: (none)

